# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Revision pipeline (Diploma_Johansson_EKF_MPC_KAN/revision)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Source, result JSONs, datasets and trained models ARE tracked: they back every
# number in the paper.  What follows is regenerable by re-running the numbered
# stage scripts, and is excluded to keep the clone small.

# Closed-loop trajectories rebuilt by s05_scenarios.py (~13 MB, 65 files)
Diploma_Johansson_EKF_MPC_KAN/revision/results/traj/

# Figures rebuilt by s06_make_figures.py (also written into the paper tree)
Diploma_Johansson_EKF_MPC_KAN/revision/figures/

# Stage logs
Diploma_Johansson_EKF_MPC_KAN/revision/*.log

# pykan writes training checkpoints to ./model relative to the working
# directory.  NOTE the near-collision: "model/" is pykan scratch and is
# ignored; "models/" holds the trained surrogates and IS tracked.
Diploma_Johansson_EKF_MPC_KAN/model/
Diploma_Johansson_EKF_MPC_KAN/revision/model/
